  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "Passive: normal attacks apply Panic stacks to target; Active: slash panicked target, dealing damage and self-healing",
    "skill1": "multiple sword techniques at appropriate range cost energy",
    "skill2": "gain a shield and increase ally ATK SPD at battle start",
    "skill3": "battle ATK speed increase",
    "skill4": "counter incoming ultimate damage with free parry counter",
    "skill5": "while shielded gain bonus energy from normal attacks"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Valka]] applies Panic stacks through normal attacks, then slashes panicked targets for damage and self-healing on ultimate. Multiple sword techniques cost Energy and give flexible offense from melee to mid-range. At battle start, a shield and ally ATK SPD boost support nearby partners while [[Valka]] pressures enemies. Battle ATK SPD growth keeps the rotation fluid, and a free parry counter punishes incoming ultimate damage. While shielded, normal attacks recover bonus Energy; enemies that deny Panic buildup or burst through the shield blunt her kit.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Valka]] opens with a shield and ally ATK SPD, then turns Panic stacks into a fast true-damage ultimate that heals her while Unaffected. Do not interrupt that cast or feed Soulshock Riposte with ultimates into her range. Catch the ultimate with [[Lily May]], delete [[Valka]] before Panic completes with true-damage melee like [[Himmel]] or [[Zorya]], and cut self-healing with [[filter:heal-inhibitor]] like [[Frieren]] or [[Gwyneth]]. Lasting [[Shemira]] pressure from outside riposte range is safer than repeated ultimates into her parry."
}
